WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:01.950
Your program won't run.

2
00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:06.910
All you get is a wall of text, and
your file has no line numbers to count.

3
00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:09.770
Now open the same code in an IDE.

4
00:00:09.820 --> 00:00:13.410
A message pops up: the
problem is on line 4.

5
00:00:13.460 --> 00:00:16.490
How did it know exactly
which line to point at?

6
00:00:16.540 --> 00:00:20.430
In this mission, you'll see that
an IDE puts tools for writing,

7
00:00:20.480 --> 00:00:24.590
translating, running and
debugging code in one place.

8
00:00:24.640 --> 00:00:27.510
Its editor numbers the lines
and colours the keywords,

9
00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:29.510
so code is easier to read.

10
00:00:29.560 --> 00:00:34.210
And it has a built-in translator, so you
can compile or interpret your code with

11
00:00:34.260 --> 00:00:35.450
one click.

12
00:00:35.500 --> 00:00:39.920
Your mission: explain how a program
can tell you which line your bug is on.
